  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Somu went to the gym today. He decided to do XXX sets of squats. Each set consists of 151515 squats. Determine the total number of squats that he did today.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains a single integer TTT — the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nThe first and only line of each test case contains an integer XXX — the total number of sets of squats that Somu did.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the total number of squats done by Somu.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤10001 \\leq T \\leq 10001≤T≤1000",
      "1≤X≤1051 \\leq X \\leq 10^51≤X≤105"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n1\n4\n99",
        "output": "15\n60\n1485",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1: Since, he does only 111 set of squats, the total number of squats done by him is 151515.\nTest Case 2: Since, he does 444 sets of squats, the total number of squats is 15+15+15+15=6015 + 15 + 15 + 15 = 6015+15+15+15=60."
      }
    ]
  },
